# =============================================================================
# 080-custom-homepage.patch — PyreVixen: Firefox Home / blank / custom URL
#
# WHAT THIS DOES
#   Adds a real custom-homepage feature (Fenix 158 has none — "homepage" upstream
#   only means the in-app home screen / opening-screen behavior):
#     * Default home screen (about:home, current behaviour)
#     * Blank page (about:blank)
#     * Custom web address (user-typed URL, https:// prepended when missing)
#   New string prefs: pref_key_homepage_mode, pref_key_homepage_custom_url
#   (values/preference_keys.xml) + typed Settings.kt properties (homepageMode,
#   homepageCustomUrl, stringPreference delegates like the neighboring props).
#   UI: a "Homepage" category in the existing Home settings screen
#   (res/xml/home_preferences.xml, wired in HomeSettingsFragment), with the
#   custom-URL field visible only when the custom mode is picked.
#   Routing: FenixBrowserUseCases.resolveHomepageUrl() is used by
#   addNewHomepageTab() and navigateToHomepage(), so every existing caller
#   (cold start in HomeActivity, toolbar Home button, tab tray, tab cleanup,
#   private notification, …) automatically opens the selected homepage.
#   Settings are threaded Components -> UseCases -> FenixBrowserUseCases as a
#   nullable param (default null) so existing unit tests keep compiling.
#
# VERIFIED AGAINST: FIREFOX-ANDROID_158_0_RELEASE (2026-10-14).
#   * No custom-homepage-URL plumbing exists upstream (verified in Settings.kt,
#     HomeSettingsFragment.kt, FenixBrowserUseCases.kt): the homepage is always
#     ABOUT_HOME_URL (concept-engine) and the only user choice is the
#     opening-screen behavior (shouldStartOnHome / enableHomepageAsNewTab).
#   * Pref keys in this tree are literal strings in values/preference_keys.xml
#     (e.g. line 452: pref_key_home); Settings.kt uses the
#     appContext.getPreferenceKey(R.string.*) + stringPreference delegate
#     pattern (e.g. toolbarSimpleShortcutKey).
#   * Home settings UI is res/xml/home_preferences.xml (androidx.preference,
#     keys as @string/pref_key_*), code-wired in
#     HomeSettingsFragment.setupPreferences() via requirePreference.
#   * FenixBrowserUseCases.addNewHomepageTab / navigateToHomepage are the two
#     central homepage entry points (12 call sites total).
#
# DELIBERATE DEVIATIONS FROM THE FIRST DRAFT
#   * No new fragment/XML/file: the UI extends the existing home_preferences.xml
#     + HomeSettingsFragment instead of inventing a HomepageSettingsFragment
#     (which would also need nav-graph wiring). No raw SharedPreferences keys:
#     the feature uses the tree's own pref-key + Settings.kt conventions.
#   * The first draft's "use homepage for new tabs" toggle is dropped: the
#     task spec covers mode + custom URL routing only; intercepting the
#     new-tab (+) button path is a separate follow-up.
#   * shouldStartOnHome() itself is unchanged: it decides home-vs-last-tab,
#     orthogonal to what "home" is.
#   * New UI strings are fork-owned literals in the XML (not @string refs);
#     move them to strings.xml when localizing.
#
# CONFIDENCE
#   * All hunks CONFIDENT — contexts copied verbatim from the 158.0 tree,
#     verified with `git apply --check`.
#   * Behavior (not patch-text) caveats for the first CI build: ListPreference
#     defaultValue/persistDefaultIfNotExists interplay; verify the mode summary
#     and URL normalization on a real device.
# =============================================================================

